ar.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2020 Q3","e":"trgp","d":"2020-11-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Christine Cho","x":"Is the initial thought that the cost savings is going to enable more production with the same amount of spending or does the pro forma entity just pocket the savings and could there be other commercial opportunities as it relates to either new contracts or modifying existing ones?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2020 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2021-02-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jen Kneale","x":"Through extensive cost reduction efforts, in 2020 we achieved significant aggregate expense savings versus our plan and we expect many of these savings to carry forward into 2021 and beyond particularly related to labor.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2020 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2021-02-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jen Kneale","x":"In the fourth quarter we redeemed our $125 million of 9% preferred units at CRP and will benefit from interest and administrative cost savings.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2021 Q1","e":"trgp","d":"2021-05-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Shneur Gershuni","x":"Or is rightsizing the dividend something on the radar screen?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2021 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2022-02-24","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jen Kneale","x":"During the fourth quarter, we recognized an approximate $452 million non-cash pretax impairment charge of our South Texas assets attributable to a lower outlook on future volumes.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2022 Q3","e":"trgp","d":"2022-11-03","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jeremy Tonet","x":"…the results quarter because if you look at the last guide and we overlay kind of the commodities how they changed and what your sensitivities were it seemed to put some pressure on EBITDA expectations for the year possibly below the bottom end, yet you were able to reaffirm the guidance range.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2023 Q1","e":"trgp","d":"2023-05-04","l":"guidance","r":"analyst","s":"Jeremy Tonet","x":"And then just wanted to dive in a little bit more on reaffirming the guidance here even with the big move in commodity prices.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2023 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2024-02-15","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Neel Mitra","x":"And then second, with the NGL pipe build oversupply, do you see your need for expanding pipe elongated just because you're able to hold your pricing power when others are competing for barrels?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2024 Q2","e":"trgp","d":"2024-08-01","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Matt Meloy","x":"Yes, we raised our guidance for this year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2024 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2025-02-20","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Matt Meloy","x":"Just kind of the talk of tariffs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2024 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2025-02-20","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Matt Meloy","x":"We've actually worked with some of the on some of our projects working in supplying US steel, so we aren't subject to the tariff.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"TRGP 2024 Q4","e":"trgp","d":"2025-02-20","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Jen Kneale","x":"That's one of the reasons that in 2024, you saw us increase our guidance range in August, then you saw us in November say we thought we'd be at the high en